==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ar|en}} {{term|حسین|tr=ḥusayn|lang=ar}}, from the root {{ar-root|ح|س|ن}}.

===Alternative forms===
* [[Husain]], [[Husein]], [[Hussain]], [[Hussein]], [[Huseyn]], [[Husseyn]], Husayn, [[Hussayn]], [[Husseyin]], [[Huseyin]]/[[Hüseyin]]
* [[Hoseyn]], [[Hosseyn]], [[Hosein]], [[Hossein]], [[Hosain]], [[Hossain]], [[Hosayn]], [[Hossayn]]
* [[Housseine]], [[Houssein]], [[Houssain]], [[Houssayn]], [[Housseyn]]

===Proper noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{context|Islam|lang=en}} A son of [[Ali]] and brother of [[Hassan]]; a [[martyr]], and [[Shiah]] [[Imam]].
# {{given name|male|from=Arabic}} used by [[Muslim]]s, diminutive of Hasan {{term|lang=ar|حسن}} meaning ''[[good]]'' or ''[[handsome]]''.
# {{surname|[[Muslim]]|from=Arabic|dot=}} derived from the {{etyl|ar|en}} given name.

